<title>ITALY: Telecom Italia announces big 96 profit rise. [CORRECTED 20:46 GMT]</title>
<headline>Telecom Italia announces big 96 profit rise. [CORRECTED 20:46 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			 2,119 vs 1,379</p>
<p>(Corrects 1995 figure to 1,379 from 1,745)</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			   4,274 vs 4,104</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	     15,415 vs 16,136</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit		 5,521 vs 5,889</p>
<p>    Cons cashflow			  11,184 vs 10,906</p>
<p>    Ord div				     125 vs 120</p>
<p>    Savings share div			145  vs 140</p>
<p>    Cons turnover			  29,376 vs 28,328</p>
<p>    Investments			     9,089 vs 7,880</p>
<p>    Net financial debt		  11,929  vs 14,787</p>
<p>    Financial charge			 971  vs 1,524</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charges		   276 vs 261</p>
<p>    Group net assets		    23,002 vs 21,882</p>
<p>    Return on equity	     9.4 percent vs 8 percent</p>
<p>Note - Telecom Italia said figures are net of satellite and mobile phone activities.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
